    "title": "Callao (2026) - All You SHOULD Know Before Going (with Reviews)",
    "text": "What is Travelers’ Choice?Tripadvisor gives a Travelers’ Choice award to accommodations, attractions and restaurants that consistently earn great reviews from travelers and are ranked within the top 10% of properties on Tripadvisor.Explore different ways to experience this place.Callao and other featured experiencesAre you currently on your trip?Help us find experiences available for you.The area ReviewsReviews are the subjective opinion of Tripadvisor members and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.Most recentReviews ordered by most recent publish date in descending order.Detailed reviewsReviews ordered by recency and descriptiveness of user-identified themes such as wait time, length of visit, general tips, and location information.What's not to love about LimaMar 2025 • CouplesJoined a cruise excursion that took in the Plaza Mayor City Square and Cathedral. There was lots of security and armed Police everywhere which I always find a bit disconcerting. Beautiful buildings and a good atmosphere despite the security. The Gold museum was really interesting, the Cathedral beautiful. Later in the day we did the Inca markets which were amazing - a little bit of everything.Written January 29, 2026This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.A quick 30 minute tripDec 2025We took a drive from Lima to look at this port. It’s definitely rather touristy in certain areas and scary and others. There is a central area near the church, which is a lovely street to walk on for about 50 yards. You can imagine movies being filmed here however, once you get past that, there’s extremely loud music that is blasting in your ear. It was good to drive around, but I wouldn’t necessarily get out and walk.Written December 17, 2025This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.Avoid CallouFeb 2024 • CouplesMy wife and I took a taxi from the airport to the old Spanish fort (Fortaleza Real). The drive there was through dilapidated streets and the industrial area around the port. The tour of the fort and its history was fine. But the area immediately surrounding the fort is really sketchy. At 4pm on a Saturday, almost directly in front if the Callou Municipal Building, we were accosted by a man panhandling who showed us a gun in his waistband. We felt lucky he did nothing more. Listen to all the other reviews here about potential danger. Go with a trusted guide or, better yet, don't go at all.Written February 18, 2024This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.JnVSydneyGreater Sydney, Australia36,183 contributionsQuick visit....Jan 2023 • CouplesDue to the troubles, we were unable to travel any further than the port, however, the market on the pier, was fun to have a browse in, and grab some arty souvenirs, and the mandatory T-shirt, at good prices, considering we were on a cruiseship. Written April 3, 2023This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.Susan CLondon, United Kingdom324 contributionsElaborate and tasteful souvenirsFeb 2023 • FriendsThe cruise terminal quayside offered a range of high quality souvenirs. From alpaca woollen throws, in all colours to super soft, toy llama. A good range of carefully crafted jewellery. Friendly vendors who did not crowd or hassle the shoppers. Great to support such local artisans while Lima and further afield remained off limits.Written March 27, 2023This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.RayICueCornelius, North Carolina4,159 contributionsJust don’t stop , keep driving into LimaFeb 2023 • CouplesA get off and get on ship spot . Otherwise not likely to be in the area . Area isn’t a scenic drive , but a real world look into the working and normal day to day activities. Lots of repairs needed, theme viewed .Written February 16, 2023This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.Not worth you pay for the tripJul 2022 • CouplesAll the wall art was crumbling down and it is basically nothing more than 1 street. The traffic and the state of the houses beyond there streets are horrible. Some of the houses were even collapsed. Very poor neighbourhood. Our advice: skip it.Written July 29, 2022This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.Plan for a successful tripAug 2021 • SoloIdeally you want to plan your trip to this area. There are some roof terrace restaurants overlooking the sea and port, the street art, the Fort and a boat trip to the island. This will be an enjoyable day. Everyone is warned to leave the area before dark. There are areas of poverty outside of the cultural zone. But I think you can have a very nice day here. Written August 16, 2021This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.Callao is still a disasterJan 2020It's a shame that both the port and airport are located in Callao because compared with most of the rest of Lima, Callao is an absolute disaster. Famous for its high levels of crime, this is not where you want tourists disembarking. The airport itself is safe, but driving out of Callao is a bad first experience. Tourists must NEVER walk the streets at night here. Just drive out as fast as you can. Don't let Callao taint your view of the rest of Lima.Written March 2, 2020This review is the subjective opinion of a Tripadvisor member and not of Tripadvisor LLC. Tripadvisor performs checks on reviews as part of our industry-leading trust & safety standards. Read our transparency report to learn more.Showing results 1-10 of 47*Likely to sell out: Based on Viator’s booking data and information from the provider from the past 30 days, it seems likely this experience will sell out through Viator, a Tripadvisor company.Is this your Tripadvisor listing?Own or manage this property? Claim your listing for free to respond to reviews, update your profile and much more.Claim your listing",
